+### Canonical paged buffer addresses
+
+`BindState::paged_addresses` selects variants that can read immutable 4 KiB page-address tables.
+A `BoundBuffer::Buffer` or `UsedResource` whose `page_table` is true gives the table's device
+address in `device_address`; `ResidentRange::paged` describes the corresponding dynamic root.
+Their presence also selects this variant automatically. Set the state flag before planning if
+resources made resident later may use tables, as the runtime's immutable `DeviceOptions::cpu_shadow`
+mode does. A paging-capable pipeline can use ordinary linear roots and paged roots together.
+
+The root entry remains four 64-bit words: `host`, `guest`, `size`, `bind_offset`. For a paged
+root, bit 63 of `size` is set; the other bits are the padded logical length, and `host` names
+an array of 64-bit canonical device addresses, one per 4096 logical bytes. The first table
+page may include a prefix before the buffer's byte zero; `guest` names that page's logical
+start and `bind_offset` includes the prefix. The table and all addressed pages remain live
+through execution. Each memory word resolves its own page, including scalar, vector and
+copy operations that cross a page boundary. Aligned atomics resolve their canonical word.
+Out-of-range accesses select the sink before any page-table load.
+
+Resident normalization preserves the original origin of a partially overlapping paged range.
+Entries still have increasing starts and ends; the search selects the last start at or below
+the guest address, then checks the masked byte length. Linear ranges retain their existing
+normalization and default shader encoding. The extra variant participates in shader cache keys.
+
 ### Snapshot reads
 
 A draw that reads, at its fragments' own pixels, a texture its own subpass renders can read it
