+- **Explicit CPU-shadow memory serializes device batches and copies their live ranges.**
+  `DeviceOptions::cpu_shadow`, off by default, keeps ordinary file memory authoritative while
+  shaders use shared canonical Vulkan storage through 4 KiB page tables. Before each batch it
+  snapshots the union of every live view's file ranges, including views retained by earlier
+  command buffers; after GPU completion it scans those ranges and writes only changed bytes
+  back before publishing events or running host steps. Canonical allocations cover at most
+  1 MiB of a file each. Fragmented fixed-function views additionally gather to scratch and
+  merge byte changes around their commands. No narrower per-command CPU snapshot or concurrent
+  shadow-batch scheduling is implemented. Sources must preserve physical file identity and
+  continuity within each logical 4 KiB page; unsupported page layouts, cross-backend rebinds,
